The PromptOpt application in the PROD environment has been experiencing degraded performance since 2026-04-27, as indicated by the `promptopt_queue_warning` detection rule triggered due to a queue depth of 150 exceeding the warning threshold of 100. Logs confirm that the daily token quota for PromptOpt was exhausted on 2026-04-27 at 16:46 UTC, causing all optimization requests to fail until midnight UTC. Additionally, on 2026-04-29, a latency spike of 1,850ms was observed, likely due to Azure OpenAI throttling, contributing to the queue buildup. These issues are attributed to resource constraints and external throttling.  

**Business Impact:**  
Optimization requests are delayed or failing, potentially impacting dependent workflows and user experience.  

**Recommended Action:**  
Increase the daily token quota for PromptOpt and engage Azure OpenAI support to address throttling concerns. Monitor queue depth and latency metrics to ensure stability.
