The PromptOpt application in the PROD environment has been experiencing degraded performance since 2026-04-27 due to Azure OpenAI throttling and token quota exhaustion. Logs confirm that the daily token quota was fully consumed on 2026-04-27, resulting in 429 errors and failed optimization requests. Although the quota reset on 2026-04-28, residual impacts were observed on 2026-04-29, including latency spikes (1,850ms vs. 1,000ms threshold) and queue depth warnings (150 vs. 100 threshold). This has disrupted PromptOpt's ability to handle optimization requests efficiently.  

**Business Impact:**  
The incident may delay optimization processes, potentially affecting dependent workflows and user experience.  

**Recommended Action:**  
Investigate Azure OpenAI quota management and throttling configurations to prevent recurrence. Consider implementing proactive monitoring and scaling measures to mitigate future impacts on PromptOpt operations.
