The ASCM application in the PROD environment has been experiencing repeated failures since 2026-04-29, impacting the ASCM Daily Data Check and the 'load_target_frequency' job. Logs indicate Oracle database connectivity issues on host `ascm-prod-ora.uniper.energy:1521`, including listener failures (ORA-12541), connection timeouts (ORA-12170), and expired access tokens. These disruptions have resulted in data unavailability and processing delays, affecting scheduled jobs and health checks. The root cause appears to be instability in the Oracle ERP system or its network configuration. Recommended action: Investigate and resolve Oracle database connectivity issues, including listener configuration and token management, to restore system stability.
